{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1044444-a-new-antagonist-idea","id":1044444,"title":"A new antagonist idea","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-06T05:05:23-08:00","id":1044444,"title":"A new antagonist idea","content":"I thought up a new antagonist for Werewolf. It is basically a small town in Louisiana that caught what I call Innsmouth Syndrome. But, instead of Dagon, they worship Eater of Souls. The town is located in the Louisiana bayou and is populated by mostly Cajuns.<br /> <br /> The town is led by Rev John Corwin, a wyrm cultist who actually infiltrated the Catholic Church. He encourages the townspeople to do foul rituals in the Wyrm's name. The worst being cannibalism. Some of the townsfolk have already mutated into formori but, visitors assume they are just inbred.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think so far?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T06:16:12-08:00","id":1044466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1044444-a-new-antagonist-idea#post1044444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I thought up a new antagonist for Werewolf. It is basically a small town in Louisiana that caught what I call Innsmouth Syndrome. But, instead of Dagon, they worship Eater of Souls. The town is located in the Louisiana bayou and is populated by mostly Cajuns.<br /> <br /> The town is led by Rev John Corwin, a wyrm cultist who actually infiltrated the Catholic Church. He encourages the townspeople to do foul rituals in the Wyrm's name. The worst being cannibalism. Some of the townsfolk have already mutated into formori but, visitors assume they are just inbred.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think so far?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds perfectly workable. I'm not sure how much different it is than most &quot;normal&quot; Wyrm cults. But it should be fun for your players to stumble upon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T09:29:46-08:00","id":1044562,"title":"","content":"How do they ritually prepare their meals?<br /> <br /> I only ask because I read a book about tribal cannibals (forgot the name off thwe top of my head) , and there are some pretty visiually disgusting ways cannibals have gone about preparing their meals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T12:19:40-08:00","id":1044657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1044444-a-new-antagonist-idea#post1044444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought up a new antagonist for Werewolf. It is basically a small town in Louisiana that caught what I call Innsmouth Syndrome. But, instead of Dagon, they worship Eater of Souls. The town is located in the Louisiana bayou and is populated by mostly Cajuns.<br /> <br /> The town is led by Rev John Corwin, a wyrm cultist who actually infiltrated the Catholic Church. He encourages the townspeople to do foul rituals in the Wyrm's name. The worst being cannibalism. Some of the townsfolk have already mutated into formori but, visitors assume they are just inbred.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think so far?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, a Reverend would be more a type of person to infiltrate (or start) a Protestant Church than a Catholic Church. The Catholic Church uses a more formal 'The Reverend' or 'The Reverend Father' for official correspondences and the informal 'Father' when dealing with parishioners. While priests of the Catholic Church are probably just as likely to fall to the Wyrm as anyone else in a position of power, the Catholic Church tends to keep a close eye of its priests (which is worrying considering how long the Catholic Church knew that specific priests were molesting children), so performing Wyrm rituals would be noticed rather quickly. I would suggest making it into a Holiness Church rather than a Catholic Church as there is not official hierarchy for Holiness Churches (you could even call it a Holiness Catholic Church, which would cause even further confusion).<br /> <br /> The safest way to promote Fomori creation is not to engage the townsfolk in Wyrm rituals but, instead, to get them to accidentally consume the products of corruption (people talk and word of massive Wyrm rituals will get around). Have the Reverend and a few of his more fanatical followers who have already because Fomori kidnap strangers, violate them in the first series of Wyrm rituals, sacrifice them in the second series of Wyrm rituals, defile their corpses in the third series of Wyrm rituals, and then mix their flesh with beef and pork to make sausages that are served at the church functions. The thrice contaminated sausages would taint anyone who consumed them and a few dozen of them would become Fomori every year. Heck, the Reverend might have a side business selling 'Heritage Cajun Sausages' online and be making money hand-over-fist while spreading the corruption of the Wyrm to unwitting yuppies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T13:56:05-08:00","id":1044710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1044444-a-new-antagonist-idea?p=1044657#post1044657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heck, the Reverend might have a side business selling 'Heritage Cajun Sausages' online and be making money hand-over-fist while spreading the corruption of the Wyrm to unwitting yuppies.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's so gross I love it!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T14:14:08-08:00","id":1044717,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the advice so far. I like the sausages idea and i might use it. Also, one of my original ideas was to have the cultists worship a Thunderwyrm but i did not know if that could work or not. I was also thinking of having a Leatherface-like character who can actually be reasoned with. He is basically the son of the Reverend's right-hand man who rules over his son with an iron fist. He is only doing these horrid acts because his father told him to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T08:03:43-08:00","id":1045058,"title":"","content":"Why can't they also be inbred? I mean you know they are evil... and insane... and deformed...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T08:19:31-08:00","id":1045072,"title":"","content":"I just got a vision of inbred swamp people opening up someones belly on a rickety fishing boat and using the still living persons guts to entice a juvenile thunderwyrm which is living in the muck below the water to surface .<br /> <br /> The wyrmy weirdo inbreds can then &quot;pray&quot; to the baby thunderwyrm from the shoreline or while they are hovered in the mossy trees overhanging the water.<br /> <br /> The juvenile Thunderwyrm has already eaten all of the other natural inhabitants of the swamp (gators , fish, turtles).<br /> <br /> The Thunderwyrms shit glows like balefire and floats to the surface of the swampwater giving off heat fumes from its radiation like properties.<br /> <br /> The radiation shit can be ingested for its hallucinogenic and vision granting properties.<br /> <br /> (sorry didn't mean to hijack)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T08:38:46-08:00","id":1045089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1044444-a-new-antagonist-idea?p=1045072#post1045072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just got a vision of inbred swamp people opening up someones belly on a rickety fishing boat and using the still living persons guts to entice a juvenile thunderwyrm which is living in the muck below the water to surface .<br /> <br /> The wyrmy weirdo inbreds can then &quot;pray&quot; to the baby thunderwyrm from the shoreline or while they are hovered in the mossy trees overhanging the water.<br /> <br /> The juvenile Thunderwyrm has already eaten all of the other natural inhabitants of the swamp (gators , fish, turtles).<br /> <br /> The Thunderwyrms shit glows like balefire and floats to the surface of the swampwater giving off heat fumes from its radiation like properties.<br /> <br /> The radiation shit can be ingested for its hallucinogenic and vision granting properties.<br /> <br /> (sorry didn't mean to hijack)</div> </div> </div> </div>You gots a talent for these neet ideas and images!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T08:49:42-08:00","id":1045102,"title":"","content":"Thank You dude, that means a lot!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T12:59:03-08:00","id":1045323,"title":"","content":"With the inbred part I did not do that because I thought it would be considered offensive. Also, they probably worship the Thunderwyrm as a demigod, thinking it is a avatar of Eater- of- Souls. Also, the reptilian disappearing might attract a mokole. What do you guys think of the potential Leatherface import?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T13:05:22-08:00","id":1045326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1044444-a-new-antagonist-idea?p=1045323#post1045323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the inbred part I did not do that because I thought it would be considered offensive. Also, they probably worship the Thunderwyrm as a demigod, thinking it is a avatar of Eater- of- Souls. Also, the reptilian disappearing might attract a mokole. What do you guys think of the potential Leatherface import?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it all sounds really workable. And giving a more reasonable enemy for the players to interact with on top of all of the other stuff should be fun.<br /> <br /> And a Mokole won't show up for the reptiles dying in 1 lake somewhere, if they weren't already invested in said lake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T13:13:12-08:00","id":1045331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1044444-a-new-antagonist-idea?p=1045326#post1045326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it all sounds really workable. And giving a more reasonable enemy for the players to interact with on top of all of the other stuff should be fun.<br /> <br /> And a Mokole won't show up for the reptiles dying in 1 lake somewhere, if they weren't already invested in said lake.</div> </div> </div> </div>True with the mobile. Also, I think the reason the Leatherface guy is immune to delirium is due to the fact he is well, not the brightest bulb in the box. In fact, he might be retarded. Also, I got to think of a way to make him last a whole adventure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T13:15:47-08:00","id":1045333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1044444-a-new-antagonist-idea?p=1045331#post1045331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True with the mobile. Also, I think the reason the Leatherface guy is immune to delirium is due to the fact he is well, not the brightest bulb in the box. In fact, he might be retarded. Also, I got to think of a way to make him last a whole adventure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some people are just immune. Easy enough to do without making an obvious reason. He'll, simplist way would be to give him 10 Willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T13:17:04-08:00","id":1045334,"title":"","content":"Leatherface is fine; maybe the kid is supposed to turn into something like a gorehound but he hates what the cult is pressuring him to do, maybe he even helps folks escape when he can (which is kind of at odds with his monstrous appearance). I also like the idea of the cannibals incorporating the glowing radioactive wyrmspoor into their rituals. Having a bunch of mutated/inbred freaks cavorting about the bayous at night during their feasts might spur on rumors of ghosts... leaving it up to your players to discover what the creepy phantom lights actually are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T13:50:47-08:00","id":1045358,"title":"","content":"The leatherface part is good. My concern with the deformed cultists is that they are members of a town and their leader is a minister. How could they hide their appearance from non cultist townspeople?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T09:53:44-08:00","id":1045829,"title":"","content":"ya'll check out resident evil 7? That essentially how the family spreads infection, via food.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T13:05:35-08:00","id":1045929,"title":"","content":"u<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1044444-a-new-antagonist-idea?p=1045358#post1045358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The leatherface part is good. My concern with the deformed cultists is that they are members of a town and their leader is a minister. How could they hide their appearance from non cultist townspeople?</div> </div> </div> </div>just a thought....<br /> <br /> maybe the most visibly mutated members of the congregation are viewed almost like living &quot;angels/demons&quot; or those &quot;especially marked with more favor from the wyrm&quot;. If that's the case , the more human looking members could be the gofers for those blessed by the wyrm so the more mutated members wouldn't be as exposed to those outside the cult.<br /> <br /> Or you could just say they have that hidden power thing from the fomori books","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T13:17:49-08:00","id":1045943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1044444-a-new-antagonist-idea?p=1045358#post1045358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The leatherface part is good. My concern with the deformed cultists is that they are members of a town and their leader is a minister. How could they hide their appearance from non cultist townspeople?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because, at the beginning of the story and the fact that everyone knows each other, they are all corrupted or in fear of their lives or just sort of confused and dealing with it as it comes day to day, but too late and dwindling days. Some people don't run when things start to go socially sour these days... when they should. They just sit down and listen to the explanations of other people's lies which might have a calming effect on a person's fears, especially if they have known that person all their life. I am just saying, it's too late at this point for everyone in that village/town, faith and social structures of &quot;belief&quot; have grasped everyone, and they sort of like this new thing, butttt, it's just too late because it's right in front of your face and grabbing onto you and you have no way out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5256-aeternal","name":"Aeternal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T16:53:19-08:00","id":1046069,"title":"","content":"They could keep the hideous members hidden in the church. Also, the minister's grandfather could have been a member of The Society of the Weeping Moon and the grandson is doing rituals found in granpop's old esoteric tomes. Also, what could attract Garou to a small town in the Louisiana bayou?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T17:02:43-08:00","id":1046074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1044444-a-new-antagonist-idea?p=1046069#post1046069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, what could attract Garou to a small town in the Louisiana bayou?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits. A vision. A Strider. A Corax. Chance. Missing kinfolk or Garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T18:27:16-08:00","id":1046104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1044444-a-new-antagonist-idea?p=1046074#post1046074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirits. A vision. A Strider. A Corax. Chance. Missing kinfolk or Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good ideas. I could do either the Strider or the the missing kin. Also, Mr. Leatherface import might try to attack the character after his father told him too. My question is how he could possibly survive the attack and help them out later?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T18:38:54-08:00","id":1046106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1044444-a-new-antagonist-idea?p=1046104#post1046104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good ideas. I could do either the Strider or the the missing kin. Also, Mr. Leatherface import might try to attack the character after his father told him too. My question is how he could possibly survive the attack and help them out later?</div> </div> </div> </div>Humans don't fight Garou and walk away. I think the best solution is to not have him fight them at all. Avert the blow at the last second as Leatherface embeds his giant weapon in the nearest tree, and breaks down sobbing about how he 'don't want to kill no more, no matter what papa says.'<br /> <br /> Maybe even ask the players for help straight up after that, if they are still entertaining thoughts of going chainsaw claws on him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T18:43:10-08:00","id":1046110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1044444-a-new-antagonist-idea?p=1046106#post1046106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Humans don't fight Garou and walk away. I think the best solution is to not have him fight them at all. Avert the blow at the last second as Leatherface embeds his giant weapon in the nearest tree, and breaks down sobbing about how he 'don't want to kill no more, no matter what papa says.'<br /> <br /> Maybe even ask the players for help straight up after that, if they are still entertaining thoughts of going chainsaw claws on him.</div> </div> </div> </div>So basically, don't have him attack at all and fling his ax away and agree the help the players? That could work very much. I am also picturing the climax being a massive ceremony in a swamp which is basically a cannabalistc feast hosted by the reverend. How would garou react to seeing canabalism?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T19:31:08-08:00","id":1046128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1044444-a-new-antagonist-idea?p=1046104#post1046104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Good ideas. I could do either the Strider or the the missing kin. Also, Mr. Leatherface import might try to attack the character after his father told him too. My question is how he could possibly survive the attack and help them out later?</div> </div> </div> </div>Striders are good for this sort of thing. It's somewhat cliche, but that's sort of their thing. With the kinfolk idea on the other hand, you can have one of the players be personally invested.<br /> <br /> Agreeing with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3695_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3695\" data-vbnamecard=\"3695\">The Laughing Stranger</a> mostly. If your NPC picks a fight with them somewhere public, he might be able to get away with it (and that would probably be a fairly non lethal fight). But if this is in the woods somewhere, definitely go with a non fight scenario.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1044444-a-new-antagonist-idea?p=1046110#post1046110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> How would garou react to seeing canabalism?</div> </div> </div> </div>They'd be enraged enough to want to end it. Grant them a Rage point as they take in the scene. If there is someone they know involved, maybe ask for a Frenzy check from any of the Garou with personal ties (maybe they find their missing kinfolk in this scene).<br /> Honestly, by the time Garou reach significant Rank they are going to see stuff like this. It isn't a matter of <i>if</i> they will, it's just a matter of <i>when</i>? For your players, this is that time for them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T19:48:44-08:00","id":1046137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1044444-a-new-antagonist-idea?p=1046128#post1046128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Striders are good for this sort of thing. It's somewhat cliche, but that's sort of their thing. With the kinfolk idea on the other hand, you can have one of the players be personally invested.<br /> <br /> Agreeing with <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> mostly. If your NPC picks a fight with them somewhere public, he might be able to get away with it (and that would probably be a fairly non lethal fight). But if this is in the woods somewhere, definitely go with a non fight scenario.<br /> <br /> <br /> They'd be enraged enough to want to end it. Grant them a Rage point as they take in the scene. If there is someone they know involved, maybe ask for a Frenzy check from any of the Garou with personal ties (maybe they find their missing kinfolk in this scene).<br /> Honestly, by the time Garou reach significant Rank they are going to see stuff like this. It isn't a matter of <i>if</i> they will, it's just a matter of <i>when</i>? For your players, this is that time for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The leatherface guy will probably be useful. But, would the Garou spare a deformed man like him who knew what the cultists were doing but did nothing to stop them? Also, perhaps the Garou would be attracted to the town after rumors of The Society of the Weeping Moon making a comeback in the towb","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T20:25:50-08:00","id":1046149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1044444-a-new-antagonist-idea?p=1046137#post1046137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The leatherface guy will probably be useful. But, would the Garou spare a deformed man like him who knew what the cultists were doing but did nothing to stop them? Also, perhaps the Garou would be attracted to the town after rumors of The Society of the Weeping Moon making a comeback in the towb</div> </div> </div> </div>If you have players interested in playing characters that are multidimensional then quite possibly.<br /> You can even give the guy the &quot;Immune to Wyrm Emanations&quot; Merit. This would be someone trapped here, unable to leave due to his deformity and who legitimately wants to help end what's going on but had no way to do it before the PCs showed up. If that isn't a person worth sparing, I don't know what is. Especially if he's managed to avoid becoming (more than mildly) tainted himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T20:36:11-08:00","id":1046152,"title":"","content":"What is the Society of the Weeping Moon, something to do with tomes and esoteria? Where can I find that in the published products? I am just getting back into W:tA and haven't read that before unless it was a long time ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5256-aeternal","name":"Aeternal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T21:18:14-08:00","id":1046167,"title":"","content":"Wild West: Frontier Secrets has stuff about the Weeping Moon. I love these guys as antagonists- they are squishy and largely worthless in a fight, but the amount of misery they can cause Garou indirectly is what makes them formidable. Also they are creepy as heck, which is another point in their favor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T02:12:59-08:00","id":1046221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1044444-a-new-antagonist-idea?p=1045072#post1045072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just got a vision of inbred swamp people opening up someones belly on a rickety fishing boat and using the still living persons guts to entice a juvenile thunderwyrm which is living in the muck below the water to surface .<br /> <br /> The wyrmy weirdo inbreds can then &quot;pray&quot; to the baby thunderwyrm from the shoreline or while they are hovered in the mossy trees overhanging the water.<br /> <br /> The juvenile Thunderwyrm has already eaten all of the other natural inhabitants of the swamp (gators , fish, turtles).<br /> <br /> The Thunderwyrms shit glows like balefire and floats to the surface of the swampwater giving off heat fumes from its radiation like properties.<br /> <br /> The radiation shit can be ingested for its hallucinogenic and vision granting properties.<br /> <br /> (sorry didn't mean to hijack)</div> </div> </div> </div>OT, but it's super weird to see you say this: the current plot in my chronicle involves deranged inbred Wyrm-cultists (led by a Skin Dancer) worshipping a radiation-fattened slumbering Thunderwyrm. The Skin Dancer wants to become a full-fledged Garou but knows Gaian werewolves will never accept him; he's trying to awaken the Thunderwyrm to get the attention/admiration of a nearby Hive. All takes place near an old atomic testing ground. The pack (as planned) thinks the Skin Dancer and his cronies are the real threat; they have no idea, muahaha. Had to come up with <i>something</i> to challenge a pack that counts a big ol Mokole amongst its ranks... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway! I love bayou settings, I always wanted to run a chronicle out of New Orleans. Sounds good, dude. Let us know how it goes!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12920-anomalocaris","name":"anomalocaris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T04:50:07-08:00","id":1046248,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the compliment. The town itself is called Mosswood, due to the fact moss hangs off every tree there. The town's economy is mostly fishing but back in the 1800s, they hunted gators for their skin and meat. The town is medium sized and has a population of 1,000. I should also mention the fact that the minister who leds the cult lived in the town all of his life and lived with his Grandpa, who used to be a Society of the Weeping Moon member. Which leds me to another question. Could it be possible to have Society tomes survive in a abandoned Society lodge for Mr. Crazy Minister to find?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T05:44:59-08:00","id":1046263,"title":"","content":"Not unless they were created from materials designed to resist decay and rot with Alchemy and/or Enchantment. Books tend to disintegrate in just a few years if they are neglected in humid and hot environments like Louisiana, though the exact rate of decay depends on the material. Rag paper was replaced by pulp paper in the majority of non-formal uses by the 1850s, so books made in the mid-19th century might be made of rag paper. Even so, the heat and humidity of Louisiana would have likely been fatal to the texts without proper care. Now, if Alchemy and/or Enchantment was used to preserve the books, the books could have survived without difficulty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T07:01:40-08:00","id":1046294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1044444-a-new-antagonist-idea?p=1046248#post1046248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Could it be possible to have Society tomes survive in a abandoned Society lodge for Mr. Crazy Minister to find?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Yes it could. That's the sort of stuff that makes for good story, and so it can certainly happen. No additional magic needed. The minister may be found the books wrapped up, hidden away. Don't feel the need to get bogged down by what paper it was written on and whether or not that can survive 150 years in Louisiana. Those details shouldn't matter (like at all) to your story.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T13:23:26-08:00","id":1046452,"title":"","content":"Even if technically the local environment should have destroyed the books and paper, this is precisely the time to imply possible supernatural influence in its preservation. So even if players think, 'Wait, shouldn't the book's pages have been destroyed by the heat and humidity?&quot; you can reply, &quot;Yes, most likely it should have been rendered unreadable.&quot; They'll think of all sorts of horrible reasons why it was preserved. You don't even need to go through the bother of saying someone mortal used alchemy or other magic. If some Bane wants it preserved, it'll be preserved against the odds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T13:37:47-08:00","id":1046459,"title":"","content":"I can see a bane preserving blasphemous book like The Society's . That would technically make the minister a sorcerer, which could make him more threatening than the average cultists. I just though up of a scene where the players eat some of the minister's sausages only to find out later they are made out of ground up human","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T13:37:51-08:00","id":1046460,"title":"","content":"If you want to really go into the Innsmouth feel, you may want to use other elements of the story. The reason the Deep Ones so heavily infiltrated the town is that initially the human collaborators prospered very much from their association. Deep Ones brought gold and good fishing to the town. So you may want to think of how this Eater of Souls cult initially got a hold in Mosswood. Perhaps it allowed them to &quot;consume&quot; the local wetlands and turn it into valuable agricultural land (which will be lost if the Eater of Souls is not kept placated), or that hunting in the swamps is particularly easy under his blessing. Perhaps the town should have been swallowed by a local sinkhole or the sea, but hasn't because the Eater of Souls is choosing not to &quot;eat&quot; the town because of its sacrifices (this would be good as an easy way to discard of any Veil breaking evidence once the PCs triumph - just have the entire town be swallowed up the earth).<br /> <br /> Since this is a cannibal cult, you may also want to bring in the various man eating cults of the Garou tribes. Perhaps there are Bone Gnawers who belong to the man eater &quot;camp&quot; nearby. They may or may not be directly tied to the Mosswood cult, but they are impacted by its corruption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T13:41:53-08:00","id":1046463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1044444-a-new-antagonist-idea?p=1046460#post1046460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to really go into the Innsmouth feel, you may want to use other elements of the story. The reason the Deep Ones so heavily infiltrated the town is that initially the human collaborators prospered very much from their association. Deep Ones brought gold and good fishing to the town. So you may want to think of how this Eater of Souls cult initially got a hold in Mosswood. Perhaps it allowed them to &amp;quot;consume&amp;quot; the local wetlands and turn it into valuable agricultural land (which will be lost if the Eater of Souls is not kept placated), or that hunting in the swamps is particularly easy under his blessing. Perhaps the town should have been swallowed by a local sinkhole or the sea, but hasn't because the Eater of Souls is choosing not to &amp;quot;eat&amp;quot; the town because of its sacrifices (this would be good as an easy way to discard of any Veil breaking evidence once the PCs triumph - just have the entire town be swallowed up the earth).<br /> <br /> Since this is a cannibal cult, you may also want to bring in the various man eating cults of the Garou tribes. Perhaps there are Bone Gnawers who belong to the man eater &amp;quot;camp&amp;quot; nearby. They may or may not be directly tied to the Mosswood cult, but they are impacted by its corruption.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like it could work finely. I was also kinda tempted to throw in a fish processing plant from Pentex's fishing subsidiary as a Easter egg. I could add in some Bone Gnawers and possibly some BSDs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T19:38:05-08:00","id":1047027,"title":"","content":"You know. I was thinking of this being the start of a werewolf's packs adventures. They would probably have their first change in Mosswood and have to fight their way through the demented congregation and clergy of Mosswood's church while slowly learning their powers. I could also post a short biography on the minister if you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}